Upstream gap: Open WebUI sends chat documents to models only as extracted text
or through its file tools, never as files, and no content extraction engine
reads text from an OpenAI-compatible Files API. Upstream closed both native
file input PRs unmerged:

https://github.com/open-webui/open-webui/pull/27627
https://github.com/open-webui/open-webui/pull/27998

With ENABLE_OPENAI_FILES_API=true and OPENAI_FILES_API_BASE_URL set, a model
whose ID, or whose workspace base model ID, matches
OPENAI_FILES_API_MODELS_REGEX_PATTERN receives each user message's documents
as standard Chat file parts with their Files API file_id, which Responses
connections send as input_file. The request's files lists drop those
documents, as for a Filter's file_handler, so retrieval and the builtin file
tools skip them. Images, audio, video, and documents whose upload fails keep
Open WebUI's usual handling. CONTENT_EXTRACTION_ENGINE=openai_files reads a
processed upload's text from GET /files/{file_id}/content?format=markdown.

Open WebUI uploads a file on first use with purpose=user_data and keeps its ID
in the file's meta as openai_file_id. Requests authenticate like the OpenAI
connection with the same base URL (get_connection_api_key from
speech-images-system-oauth.patch), send OPENAI_FILES_API_PARAMS as query
parameters, and time out after OPENAI_FILES_API_TIMEOUT seconds. Files are
never deleted from the Files API.

Removal check: an Open WebUI release that sends chat documents by Files API
file ID and extracts their text through a Files API.

